      "kicker": "02 / THE DEFINITION",
      "title": "A model is not a product — it is an input",
      "body": "An open-weight model is software you can download, inspect, modify and run on your own infrastructure. The model becomes a raw input; the product is the system around it — workflow, data, distribution, trust.",
